        "id": 216141,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-22T01:59:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Anyway…&nbsp;<strong><em>Animated Absolute Zero&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><em>Ice Spikes</em></p>\n<p><strong>Power:</strong> Absolute Zero deals 1 target 1 cold damage. Then, Absolute Zero deals a target dealt damage this way X melee damage, where X is the amount of cold damage dealt by Absolute Zero this turn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ooooof.&nbsp; Get out a single Cold Snap in a target rich environment (or even a boosted Impale or two) and that gets real broken, real quick.&nbsp; With even basic buffs, you could easily finding your base power dealing 30 damage per round or more.&nbsp; Plus, does Absolute Zero need <em>more</em> math?</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
