        "id": 216145,
        "name": "Blackfang108",
        "username": "Blackfang108",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-23T14:34:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PlatinumWarlock\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/48/1869_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> PlatinumWarlock:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Trajector wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Anyway...&nbsp;<strong><em>Animated Absolute Zero&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><em>Ice Spikes</em><strong>Power:</strong> Absolute Zero deals 1 target 1 cold damage. Then, Absolute Zero deals a target dealt damage this way X melee damage, where X is the amount of cold damage dealt by Absolute Zero this turn.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nOoooof.&nbsp; Get out a single Cold Snap in a target rich environment (or even a boosted Impale or two) and that gets real broken, real quick.&nbsp; With even basic buffs, you could easily finding your base power dealing 30 damage per round or more.&nbsp; Plus, does Absolute Zero need *more* math?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I belive that's what we call… <em>spike</em> damage.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And yes.&nbsp; Everyone can use more math.</p>",
